# v0.1.3 item 1 — SKILL.md packages bundle

2026-05-04. v0.1.3 item per `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-x-roadmap.md`
§2 v0.1.3 item 1 + Decision D (ship 5 packages) + §8
method-decision register backfill.

Sub-plan: `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-3-skill-packages.md`.

FIDRAFT entry closed (`docs/rebuild/FUTURE_IDEAS_DRAFT.md` —
captured 2026-05-03):
  - "Anthropic-perspective recommendation ladder (R.1-R.6)" —
    item R.4 (3-5 SKILL.md packages) lands here.

Scope (per sub-plan §5): single-component fence on the NEW
plugin `plugins/loam-skills/`. Second sealed component under
the `plugins/` tree (first was `dev-sdlc` at v0.1.0 M6a). Leaf
plugin — markdown-only artefact, no runtime dependencies, no
`loam.bootstrap.contributions` entry-point. Skills are
filesystem-discovered by Claude Code natively per Anthropic's
SKILL.md schema (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills).

Three AC families (all under AC.LSK.*):

  - AC.LSK.1 — five SKILL.md packages present and well-formed.
    Each file: starts with valid YAML frontmatter delimited
    by `---`; frontmatter parses as mapping; carries non-empty
    `description` field (≤1536 chars per Anthropic's combined
    cap); body (post-frontmatter) is non-empty markdown.

  - AC.LSK.2 — frontmatter follows Anthropic SKILL.md schema.
    Directory name kebab-case + ≤64 chars. If `name` field
    present, matches directory name. Description carries
    trigger-phrase clause ("use when" / "before" / "when X").
    No unknown frontmatter fields beyond `name` (optional)
    and `description` — minimal v0.1.3 surface.

  - AC.LSK.3 — body content shape. Required sections:
    `## What this skill captures`, `## When to use`,
    `## How the persona applies it`, `## Graceful degradation`,
    `## Composition`, `## Out of scope`. Body references at
    least one named loam pattern (F3, F4, ODD, M-FBM, FIDRAFT,
    Lens 1, etc.) for traceable provenance. Graceful-degradation
    section names raw-Claude-Code path explicitly.

  - AC.LSK.S — single-component fence on `plugins/loam-skills/`;
    plus `docs/rebuild/plans/` via universal prefix; plus
    `install-from-source.txt` + `docs/install-from-source.md`
    via component-level `extra_allowed_files` (Tier K append).

The 5 SKILL.md packages (per Decision D — ship 5):

  1. memory-recall — file-based memory retrieval pattern.
     Composes with M-FBM's auto-injected per-turn retrieval
     block; degrades to filesystem search for raw Claude Code.
  2. scope-decompose — F3 swarming stopping criterion.
     "Decompose if subtasks have tighter ACs; stop when split
     adds only coordination overhead."
  3. dispatch-with-gates — scope-only dispatch + halt-and-surface.
     "Pass objective + scope + constraints + halt triggers +
     ODD-check ONLY. Never enumerate files / symbols / ACs."
  4. onboarding-conversation — primary-persona greeting shape
     for fresh sessions. Surfaces what's in flight + what
     needs attention + what just completed.
  5. session-handoff — durable-capture rule before session
     close. "Files are the only memory; nothing is session-
     locked."

Smokes captured pre-seal (verbatim):

    === Smoke A (AC.LSK.1 + AC.LSK.2 — discoverability + frontmatter) ===
    All 5 SKILL.md files parse cleanly:
      memory-recall          — desc 446 chars; trigger "Use when..."
      scope-decompose        — desc 533 chars; trigger "Use when..."
      dispatch-with-gates    — desc 460 chars; trigger "Use when..."
      onboarding-conversation— desc 432 chars; trigger "Use when..."
      session-handoff        — desc 437 chars; trigger "Use when..."

    === Smoke B (AC.LSK.3 — body content shape) ===
    All 5 packages carry the standard 6-section body shape:
      ## What this skill captures
      ## When to use
      ## How the persona applies it
      ## Graceful degradation (raw Claude Code path)
      ## Composition (loam patterns referenced)
      ## Out of scope

    === Smoke C (claude-code skill discovery — pip install + walk) ===
    $ .venv/bin/pip install -e ./plugins/loam-skills
    Successfully installed loam-plugin-loam-skills-0.1.0
    $ .venv/bin/pip show loam-plugin-loam-skills | grep Version
    Version: 0.1.0
    $ find plugins/loam-skills/skills -name SKILL.md | sort
    plugins/loam-skills/skills/dispatch-with-gates/SKILL.md
    plugins/loam-skills/skills/memory-recall/SKILL.md
    plugins/loam-skills/skills/onboarding-conversation/SKILL.md
    plugins/loam-skills/skills/scope-decompose/SKILL.md
    plugins/loam-skills/skills/session-handoff/SKILL.md
    (5 files; matches Anthropic's filesystem-walk discovery rule.)

    === Smoke D (post-seal fence-clean cross-check) ===
    Run post-seal: `git diff <BASELINE>..<seal_sha> --name-only`
    confined to plugins/loam-skills/ + docs/rebuild/plans/ +
    install-from-source.txt + docs/install-from-source.md.

    === Smoke E (touched-only test pass) ===
    $ .venv/bin/python -m pytest plugins/loam-skills/tests/ -v
    43 passed in 0.06s

All ACs (AC.LSK.{1,2,3}) pass: 5 SKILL.md files exist with
well-formed frontmatter + standard body shape + named loam-
pattern provenance + graceful-degradation guidance for raw
Claude Code.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Frontmatter minimalism: only `description` (Anthropic's
    recommended minimum). `name` defaults to directory name.
    No `disable-model-invocation`, `allowed-tools`, etc — these
    are reference-content skills (knowledge applied alongside
    conversation), not task-shaped skills with side effects.
  - Body section shape mirrors existing flat-skill convention
    (`memory-search.md`, `start-project.md`) plus an explicit
    `## Graceful degradation` section so raw-Claude-Code users
    know what to do when loam infrastructure isn't present.
  - Plugin pyproject.toml has NO `loam.bootstrap.contributions`
    entry-point — skills are filesystem-discovered by Claude
    Code natively per the Anthropic schema. The pyproject
    exists solely so `pip install -e ./plugins/loam-skills`
    recognises the package.
  - Plugin is markdown-only — no Python source modules.
    `setuptools.packages = []` keeps auto-discovery from
    creating spurious top-level modules.
  - Test files mirror AC.LAE.* shape from v0.1.2 item 6
    (parametrized tests, AC-named modules, sealed-component
    partner test_no_sealed_amendments.py).
  - Tier K append in install-from-source.txt (one-line entry)
    + corresponding update in docs/install-from-source.md
    (per-component fallback section). Both admitted via
    component-level `extra_allowed_files` since they sit
    outside the plugin's subtree.

Out of scope (per sub-plan §9):

  - Migration of existing flat-shape skills
    (plugins/dev-sdlc/skills/start-project.md +
    framework/primary-persona/skills/memory-{search,archive}.md)
    to the modern directory-per-skill shape — out of fence;
    v0.2+ if Anthropic discovery requires it.
  - Live `claude` binary discovery smoke (boot-claude-in-fixture)
    — out of fence; static-walk smoke is sufficient at the
    amendment-cycle level.
  - Updating dev-mode-manifest.yaml for plugins/loam-skills/
    — `roots:` doesn't include plugins/* by default; same
    treatment as plugins/dev-sdlc/. Follow-on amendment if
    dev-mode loading wants to surface to the persona.
  - PyPI publishing — deferred to v0.2 per the broader publish
    gate.
  - A 6th SKILL package or beyond — Decision D locks at 5.
  - Reference scripts in the SKILL packages — none in v0.1.3;
    all 5 are pure markdown reference content. Can extend in
    v0.1.4+ if specific patterns benefit.

Predecessor commits:
  - 9d58062 — V11.A seal (orchestrator runtime fix).
  - 7d19a7e — V11.E seal (graphiti probe graceful-skip).
  - 32ff67d — ack-first persona contract seal.
  - 2c32c1b — loam-amend ergonomics sweep seal.
  - 7ae346d — v0.1.3 R.5 design note 1 (primary-persona-shape) seal.
  - ce58521 — v0.1.x roadmap §2 relabel (canonical pos-v2 HEAD
    pre-this-build).
  - 2c95507 — v0.1.3 item 1 sub-plan-doc (NEW commit; pre-baseline).
  - 059dc05 — v0.1.3 item 1 source-edit commit (BASELINE for this
    amendment).

BASELINE 059dc05 (the v0.1.3 item 1 source-edit commit). Single-
component fence on `plugins/loam-skills/`; sidecar advances to
v0.1.3-item-1 seal SHA at apply time. install-from-source
admissions via component-level extra_allowed_files.

# v0.1.6 Cycle 2 — 3 base SKILLs (translation-discipline +
audit-block-on-telegram + owner-decision-summary)

2026-05-04. v0.1.6 Cycle 2 per
`docs/rebuild/plans/eric-final-delivery-plan-2026-05-04.md` §2
v0.1.6 row.

Sub-plan: `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-6-production-safety-and-base-skills.md`.

Scope (per sub-plan §6 Cycle 2): single-component fence on the
`plugins/loam-skills/` plugin. Adds 3 new SKILL.md packages to
the v0.1.3 5-package bundle (sealed at `f04e925`); extends the
`EXPECTED_SKILLS` lists in the 3 AC.LSK test families.

AC families:

  - AC.SKILLS-BASE.1 — `translation-discipline` SKILL.md
    authored, frontmatter valid, body covers anti-pattern
    checklist (no commit SHAs / AC IDs / abbreviations / doc-
    section refs without summary; before-send pass).
  - AC.SKILLS-BASE.2 — `audit-block-on-telegram` SKILL.md
    authored, surface-when-meaningful logic specified
    (audit-rule refinement: surface only when ✗ / decision /
    commit / explicitly asked; thinking-block always walks
    the list).
  - AC.SKILLS-BASE.3 — `owner-decision-summary` SKILL.md
    authored, body covers Summary + Named Decisions with
    Recommendations format (prevents doc-section-pointer
    regression).
  - AC.SKILLS-BASE.4 — All 3 new + 5 existing SKILLs well-
    formed per AC.LSK.{1,2,3} test families. EXPECTED_SKILLS
    extended from 5 to 8 in each test file. 66/66 tests pass
    against the 8-package bundle (was 43 for the v0.1.3 5).
  - AC.SKILLS-BASE.5 — All 8 SKILLs auto-discoverable in
    canonical pos-v2 (smoke-test, status-file recorded).

The 8 SKILLs after this seal:

  v0.1.3 bundle (sealed at f04e925, retained):
    1. memory-recall
    2. scope-decompose
    3. dispatch-with-gates
    4. onboarding-conversation
    5. session-handoff

  v0.1.6 Cycle 2 additions (this seal):
    6. translation-discipline
    7. audit-block-on-telegram
    8. owner-decision-summary

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Each new SKILL is reference-content style (not task-content);
    no `disable-model-invocation`, no `allowed-tools`, no
    `argument-hint` — matches v0.1.3 minimal-surface convention.
  - Frontmatter carries only `description` field (Anthropic's
    recommended minimum); `name` defaults to directory name.
  - Body shape: standard 6-section template (`## What this skill
    captures`, `## When to use`, `## How the persona applies it`,
    `## Graceful degradation`, `## Composition`, `## Out of scope`).
  - Each new SKILL's body references at least one named loam
    pattern (loam, FIDRAFT, ODD, F4) for traceable provenance
    per AC.LSK.3.
  - EXPECTED_SKILLS list is extended in three test files; the
    existing parametrized tests gate the new packages
    automatically. No new test file authored — the test SHAPE
    was already correct at v0.1.3; only the constant changes.
  - The `test_all_five_skills_discovered` test is renamed to
    `test_all_skills_discovered` to reflect the 8-package
    bundle; a new `test_skills_count_eight` test pins the
    count.

Out of scope (per sub-plan §7):

  - Cycle 1 (production-safety + bug fixes) sealed at
    3f1d237 — separate manifest, predecessor of this seal.
  - dev-mode-manifest edits — defer to v0.1.7.
  - Migration of existing flat-shape skills — out of fence.
  - 6 dev-specific SKILLs from FIDRAFT (front-load-principle-walk,
    dispatch-brief-authoring, sealed-component-amendment-ship) —
    defer to plugins/dev-sdlc/skills/ at v0.1.8 / v0.1.9.

Predecessor commits:
  - f04e925 — v0.1.3 SKILL.md packages bundle seal (5 base SKILLs).
  - 3f1d237 — v0.1.6 Cycle 1 seal (production-safety + bug fixes).
  - e3e5eb4 — feat(v0.1.6): 3 base SKILLs (this BASELINE).

BASELINE e3e5eb4 — single-component fence on
`plugins/loam-skills/`. Sidecar advances to the v0.1.6 Cycle 2
seal SHA at apply time.

# loam-skills-ac-lsk1-root-cause — AC.LSK.{1,2,3} derive-from-
disk rewrite + AC.LSK.1 prose tightening

2026-05-22. Root-cause fix for the enumeration-trap defect in
the AC.LSK family that blocked Batch A's seal. Sub-plan:
`docs/plans/loam-skills-ac-lsk1-root-cause.md` (archived to
`docs/plans/sealed/` at T1.4).

Scope: single-component fence on `plugins/loam-skills/`.
Three test rewrites + one sealed-plan-doc prose tightening +
one new outcome-altitude test. No SKILL package content
changes. No pyproject changes (Batch A's territory).

Defect: `test_AC_LSK_1_skill_packages_present.py::test_all_
skills_discovered` failed because EXPECTED_SKILLS hardcoded
10 names while 20 well-formed packages exist on disk
(verified pre-flight). 10 packages added since the test was
last touched (v0.8.0 `4f1dcf6`) with no list bump:
claude-agents-view, cron-create, goal-command, handsoff-loop,
launchd-plist, loop-command, monitor-tool, precompact-hook,
run-in-background-bash, schedule-wakeup. The same enumeration-
trap exists silently in AC.LSK.2 + AC.LSK.3 tests (10
packages × 2 ACs = 20 unverified assertions); only AC.LSK.1's
cross-check surfaced the defect.

AC families (Option-1-WIDENED, turn-3 dispatcher ratification):

  - AC.LSK1RC.TEST1 — test_AC_LSK_1_skill_packages_present.py
    rewrite: derive SKILL set from disk; remove EXPECTED_
    SKILLS; remove test_skills_count_ten; per-skill well-
    formedness assertions preserved + executing against ≥20
    packages.
  - AC.LSK1RC.TEST2 — test_AC_LSK_2_frontmatter_well_formed.
    py rewrite: same derive-from-disk pattern; per-skill
    frontmatter assertions preserved.
  - AC.LSK1RC.TEST3 — test_AC_LSK_3_body_content_shape.py
    rewrite: derive-from-disk + conditional logic per the
    `is_claude_primitive_package` heuristic (presence of
    `## When to load me` OR `## What this is` H2 header
    signals primitive-subject → exempt from loam-pattern +
    graceful-degradation checks); section-shape predicate
    flexible per AC.LSK1RC.AC3.
  - AC.LSK1RC.AC1 — docs/plans/sealed/v0-1-3-skill-packages.
    md AC.LSK.1 prose tightening (lines 123-141): heading
    no longer pins count "five"; body no longer enumerates
    v0.1.3-era paths; four well-formedness criteria
    preserved; explicit derived-from-disk note added.
  - AC.LSK1RC.AC3 — docs/plans/sealed/v0-1-3-skill-packages.
    md AC.LSK.3 prose tightening (lines 153-161, Option-1-
    WIDENED): widens the three body-shape assertion families
    to admit both v0.1.3-era and post-v0.1.6 claude-primitive
    conventions; section-shape is a semantic predicate;
    loam-pattern + graceful-degradation checks are
    conditional (skipped for claude-primitive-subject
    packages).
  - AC.LSK1RC.S — outcome-altitude smoke: production-altitude
    invocation against real skills/ tree + four synthetic
    fixtures (malformed loam-pattern → fails; valid claude-
    primitive without GD → passes via exemption; empty body
    → fails; positive cases → pass). RED-on-regression proof.

Eight plan-author halt-and-surface findings (plan §10) all
surfaced + autonomous-decision-recorded:
  F1 — AC.LSK.1 text is loose, NOT load-bearing enumeration
       (fix-the-AC discipline applies per `feedback_loose_AC_
       text_fix_AC_not_implementation`).
  F2 — Scope widens from AC.LSK.1-only to AC.LSK.{1,2,3}
       (same defect class; asymmetric-problem-solving).
  F3 — meta-decision-haiku not-yet-packaged dir correctly
       excluded by per-directory SKILL.md filter.
  F4 — AC.LSK1RC.S synthetic-fixture path is the RED-on-
       regression proof (pass-only insufficient).
  F5 — Single-component fence sufficient.
  F6 — No method-in-AC trap per ODD §2.5.
  F7 — No sub-amendment split per Lens 5 stopping criterion.
  F8 — AC.LSK.3 has three assertion families, not one
       (Option-1-WIDENED; section-shape + loam-pattern +
       graceful-degradation each get conditional treatment
       via the claude-primitive heuristic).

Unblocks Batch A's seal. Sequence: A-FIX seals → Batch A
re-seals → B → C.
